north korean leader kim jong-un has  warned he is ready to use nuclear  weapons against rivals the united states  and south korea the warning came as  north koreans marked the 69th  anniversary of the armistice that ended  hostilities in the korean war this day  is known as victory day in north korea  kim's warnings come amid fears his  country is preparing to conduct a  seventh nuclear test analysts see his  latest rhetoric as an attempt to shore  up morale in a country dealing with a  covet outbreak  a faltering economy and the threat of  renewed sanctions but the celebrations  on wednesday provided no hint of any  such troubles  at pyongyang's kim il-sung square  citizens dance to mark the so-called  victory day  although the korean war in the 50s ended  in a truce for north korea it was a  victory against the u.s  nationwide celebrations already started  much earlier in the day  filling the streets with pride  we're marching towards the victorious  fatherland liberation war museum while  singing songs that the war victors used  to sing  in a speech to mark the event north  korean leader kim jong-un claimed the  country is ready for military clashes  with the u.s  this came as washington said pyongyang  could conduct a nuclear test anytime the  first since 2017.  kim said our armed forces are thoroughly  prepared to respond to any crisis and  our state's nuclear war deterrence is  also fully ready to mobilize its  absolute strength faithfully accurately  and promptly to its mission  while north korean rhetoric is often  fiery tensions have in fact been rising  on the peninsula  south korean president yun seokyo has  laid out a more aggressive defense  policy since he took office in may  it would allow seoul to launch  preemptive strikes on certain targets  which could kill kim jong-un himself  the government also warned of  consequences if the north conducts a  nuclear test  [Music]  north korea would face even stronger  sanctions if it pushes ahead with the  seventh nuclear test  a hawkish stance kim jong-un strongly  despised  on the victory day he criticized the  south korean president and branded his  administration quote a group of  gangsters  [Laughter]  but for most north koreans it wasn't a  day of fury it simply was an event of  joy pride and a lot of entertainment
 

